	'i_about_s1_h' => 'The Studio Story and Our Two Bays',
	'i_about_s1_p' => 'Ines Calloway founded Kirinuki Studio in 2014 after leaving a commercial catalogue production house. Her aim was to replace cumbersome agency layers with an independent studio built around craft, calm collaboration, and predictable pricing. Today, Kirinuki operates from Unit 4, Wharf Yard, 22 Lantern Street in Harwick, housing two specialized production spaces under one roof. Bay A features our permanent six-metre white sweep equipped with an extensive strobe and softbox rig, engineered specifically for high-volume packshot, detail, and ghost-mannequin apparel days. Bay B serves as our dedicated daylight set room, capturing soft, natural window illumination across tailored lifestyle and editorial tabletop arrangements.',
	'i_about_s2_h' => 'The Seven People Behind Every Shoot',
	'i_about_s2_p' => 'Every production at Kirinuki Studio is managed by our permanent crew of seven. Founder Ines Calloway leads studio direction and creative standards. Dev Raman acts as lead photographer for all packshot and catalogue days, while Marta Okonkwo supports as first assistant and digital technician at the tether screen. Lukas Brenner oversees lighting architecture and custom set builds. Sofia Laine leads styling, sourcing props and dressing surfaces for lifestyle set commissions in Bay B. Noor Petrova supervises all post-production as retouch lead, ensuring colour fidelity across every batch. Studio manager Theo Mbeki coordinates scheduling, handles client bookings, and leads the shot-list planning call prior to shoot day.',
	'i_about_s3_h' => 'How We Work and Our Core Studio Rules',
	'i_about_s3_p' => 'We believe commercial photography runs best when production steps are transparent and methodical. We shoot entire product batches on a single sweep in one day, reviewing and approving every initial camera angle in real time on our calibrated studio monitor. This disciplined workflow enables dependable turnaround times across every project: complete online proofing galleries delivered within three working days, followed by finished retouched master files within five working days. Our studio rules are absolute. We never charge rush fees, we never bill surprise equipment surcharges, and we never add hidden retouch fees. Clients receive honest rates, clear communication, and consistent imagery every time.',
