	'i_faq_a1' => 'We require at least two weeks\' notice to book a production day in Bay A or Bay B. When you reach out to book, studio manager Theo Mbeki will provisionally hold your chosen calendar date for 5 working days while you finalize your shot list and confirm product shipping schedules. If you have an urgent catalogue deadline, you can also join our open dates list to receive immediate notifications whenever a studio cancellation frees up an upcoming weekday bay.',
	'i_faq_a2' => 'On a standard packshot day in Bay A, our team photographs up to 60 products across two angles each on our white sweep. For smaller inventories, our packshot half day accommodates up to 25 products across two angles between 09:00 and 13:00. For clothing brands, an apparel day covers up to 45 garments front and back on our ghost mannequin rig. On lifestyle set days in Bay B, we capture 30 finished editorial images on a single styled set.',
	'i_faq_a3' => 'Yes, clients are always welcome to attend shoot days at Unit 4, Wharf Yard in Harwick. Our studio opens for load-in at 08:30, and shooting runs from 09:00 to 17:00. You can review shots alongside digital tech Marta Okonkwo at our calibrated monitor as each frame is taken. If your team cannot travel, you can attend remotely: we upload live test frames during morning setup and confirm every hero angle before executing the full batch.',
	'i_faq_a4' => 'We deliver full-resolution master TIFF or JPEG files alongside web-optimized versions cropped to your required marketplace dimensions, such as digital storefronts, product catalogue listings, or print advertising specifications. Every file undergoes basic retouching by Noor Petrova, including sensor dust clean-up, physical surface blemish removal, and accurate colour calibration against physical reference cards. If you require additional retouched images beyond what is included in your day rate package, they are billed at €14 per extra image.',
	'i_faq_a5' => 'You may cancel your shoot day free of charge up to 10 working days before your scheduled date. Cancellations made within 10 working days of the shoot incur a 50% fee to cover reserved bay time and crew commitments. Every client is permitted to move their confirmed shoot date once without penalty, provided our bookings desk receives written notice. We hold dates for 5 working days while you confirm your initial booking with Theo.',
	'i_faq_a6' => 'Our standard production hours run Monday through Friday from 08:30 to 18:00, with shooting taking place between 09:00 and 17:00. We do not maintain regular weekend operations, but Saturday shoot days can occasionally be accommodated by special arrangement for multi-day productions or time-critical brand launches. Please discuss Saturday requirements directly with studio manager Theo Mbeki during your initial booking inquiry so we can coordinate bay availability and crew schedules.',
	'i_faq_a7' => 'Turnaround times are fixed and identical across every shoot we run. You receive access to a private online proofing gallery within 3 working days following your shoot day. Once you review and approve your hero frames, our post-production team delivers the final retouched, colour-matched, and cropped master files within 5 working days. We adhere strictly to this schedule so that your e-commerce launches, marketing campaigns, and press distributions stay on track.',
	'i_faq_a8' => 'Every day rate includes unlimited commercial usage rights for the final delivered imagery for your own products, spanning your website, social media, printed packaging, and digital advertisements. Invoices are issued upon completion of the shoot and are payable within 14 days. All stated day rates exclude VAT. We never charge ongoing licensing royalties or additional usage renewals for client product photography. Once final files are delivered, you are free to use them across all brand sales channels without expiration.',
