	'i_privacy_title' => 'Privacy Policy',
	'i_rates_lede' => 'We operate on transparent, all-inclusive day rates with no hidden fees or unexpected equipment charges. Every booking includes our complete studio crew, lighting, tethered review, and retouching.',
	'i_rates_s1_p' => 'Every shoot booked at Kirinuki Studio includes our seven fixed commitments as standard: photographer and assistant; the bay 09:00–17:00; white sweep, lighting and grip; tethered capture with live review on the studio screen; basic retouch (clean-up, colour match, crop to your marketplace sizes); online gallery within 3 working days; final files within 5 working days. We do not charge separate line items for camera usage, standard lighting modifiers, or digital file storage. You know the exact cost of your production before your samples arrive at our loading bay.',
	'i_rates_s2_h' => 'Production Rates and Add-On Pricing',
	'i_rates_s2_p' => 'Our production day rates are structured around clear commercial deliverables. A Packshot day in Bay A costs €1,450 for up to 60 products across two angles on our white sweep. A Packshot half day in Bay A costs €820 for up to 25 products from 09:00 to 13:00. A Lifestyle set day in Bay B is €2,200, including one styled set, styling, props, and 30 finished images. An Apparel day in Bay A is €1,600 for up to 45 garments on a ghost mannequin, front and back. Add our Video loop add-on for €480, delivering 6 short loops of 6 seconds on the same set. Additional retouched images beyond day allowances cost €14 per image. Prices exclude VAT. A day needs 2 weeks\' notice; we hold a date for 5 working days while you confirm.',
	'i_rates_s3_h' => 'Notice Periods, Calendar Holds, and Cancellations',
	'i_rates_s3_p' => 'We ask for two weeks\' advance notice to book a production day. Once you request a date with studio manager Theo Mbeki, we hold that calendar date for 5 working days while you confirm your product list and logistics. If you need to cancel, notice received at least 10 working days prior to your shoot incurs no fee whatsoever. Cancellations made within 10 working days are billed at 50% of the day rate. Clients may reschedule their confirmed booking date once without penalty. Invoices are issued upon shoot completion and are payable within 14 days.',
	'i_rates_title' => 'Day Rates and Inclusions',
	'i_send_1' => 'Product list',
	'i_send_2' => 'Sizes and heights',
	'i_send_3' => 'Reference images',
	'i_send_4' => 'Marketplace specs',
	'i_send_5' => 'Samples and props',
	'i_send_6' => 'Preferred dates',
	'i_send_g' => 'Send with your request',
	'i_send_h' => 'What to send us',
	'i_send_sub' => 'Before the shot-list call',
	'i_shoots_lede' => 'We provide four core commercial photography formats tailored for modern product brands, digital storefronts, and printed catalogues. Each shoot is booked on a clear day or half-day rate with all essentials included.',
	'i_shoots_s1_h' => 'Packshot Days in Bay A',
	'i_shoots_s1_p' => 'Our packshot days are engineered for online stores, packaging updates, and catalogue inventories that demand uniform clarity. Staged on the six-metre white sweep in Bay A, a full packshot day accommodates up to 60 products photographed across two angles each for €1,450, while a half day covers up to 25 products from 09:00 to 13:00 for €820. Before the shoot, send us your itemized inventory, samples, and marketplace crop specifications. You receive live tethered monitor review, basic retouching, colour matching, an online review gallery within 3 working days, and final retouched files in 5 working days.',
	'i_shoots_s2_h' => 'Lifestyle Set Days in Bay B',
	'i_shoots_s2_p' => 'Lifestyle days in Bay B capture products within lived environments, using morning and afternoon window light to highlight tactile textures. Booked at €2,200 per day, this session includes one custom styled room or tabletop set, comprehensive prop sourcing by stylist Sofia Laine, and 30 finished retouched images. Prior to production, clients provide brand guidelines, mood references, and physical samples. We style compositions with hands in frame, architectural elements, and natural textures. Deliverables follow our standard studio turnaround: an online proof gallery within 3 working days and final colour-graded master files within 5 working days.',
	'i_shoots_s3_h' => 'Detail and Flat Lay Photography',
	'i_shoots_s3_p' => 'Detail and flat lay photography highlights product craft, material textures, ingredient stories, and bundled collections. Shot on Bay A\'s sweep or on textured surfaces in Bay B, these arrangements capture delicate surfaces, liquid drops, and packaging close-ups under precision macro lighting. Send us your styling notes, product pairings, and surface preferences. You receive meticulous tethered capture, true-to-life colour matching, and marketplace-ready deliverables. Detail sessions are booked as part of our packshot day rates (€1,450 for a full day or €820 for a half day), delivering online galleries within 3 working days and final files in 5 working days.',
	'i_shoots_s4_h' => 'Apparel and Motion on the Ghost Mannequin',
	'i_shoots_s4_p' => 'Our apparel sessions showcase garments with structural depth, clean collar symmetry, and crisp fabric fidelity. Billed at €1,600 per day in Bay A, an apparel day covers up to 45 garments photographed front and back on our modular ghost mannequin system. Clients can add our video loop add-on for €480, delivering 6 short loops of 6 seconds on the same set to show fabric drape and motion. Send your steamed garments and size guidelines. You receive front and back cutout-ready assets, 3-day online proofing, and final files in 5 working days.',
	'i_shoots_title' => 'Kinds of Shoot',
	'i_tab_h' => 'Day rates',
	'i_tab_sub' => 'Prices exclude VAT',
	'i_terms_lede' => 'These terms govern commercial shoot bookings, calendar date holds, payment schedules, and usage rights for all photography produced by Kirinuki Studio.',
	'i_terms_s1_h' => 'Booking Holds, Notice Requirements, and Cancellation Terms',
	'i_terms_s1_p' => 'All production bookings require at least two weeks\' advance notice. Upon receipt of a booking request, Kirinuki Studio will hold your selected calendar date for 5 working days while you confirm your product list and arrangements. Cancellations notified at least 10 working days prior to the confirmed shoot date incur no cancellation fee. Cancellations made within 10 working days of the shoot are charged at 50% of the day rate. Clients may reschedule their confirmed shoot date once without penalty.',
	'i_terms_s2_h' => 'Image Deliverables, Commercial Licensing, and Invoicing',
	'i_terms_s2_p' => 'Every shoot includes an online review gallery within 3 working days and final retouched files within 5 working days. Clients receive unlimited commercial usage rights for the final delivered images for their own products across websites, digital marketing, packaging, and point-of-sale materials. Studio invoices are issued upon completion of production and are payable within 14 days. Stated day rates exclude VAT. Kirinuki Studio retains moral authorship of all photographs created at Unit 4, Wharf Yard.',
	'i_terms_title' => 'Terms of Service',
	'i_thanks_lede' => 'Thank you for contacting Kirinuki Studio. Your shoot inquiry has been delivered directly to our Harwick production desk.',
	'i_thanks_s1_h' => 'Confirmation of Your Booking Request',
	'i_thanks_s1_p' => 'We have received your message and product details. Studio manager Theo Mbeki reviews incoming shoot requests daily and will reply within one working day. If you requested a specific shoot day in Bay A or Bay B, we will provisionally hold that calendar date for 5 working days while we discuss your shot list, sample quantities, and production logistics. Our bookings desk confirms date availability in the order inquiries arrive.',
	'i_thanks_s2_h' => 'Preparing Your Product Manifest and Samples',
	'i_thanks_s2_p' => 'While waiting for our reply, we recommend compiling your product manifest, noting dimensions, sample variants, and desired marketplace crops. If your inquiry requires immediate attention or you need to update your scheduled arrival date, feel free to contact our studio desk directly at hello@kirinuki-studio.example or telephone +00 20 7946 0412. Our studio hours are Monday through Friday, 08:30 to 18:00, at Unit 4, Wharf Yard, 22 Lantern Street in Harwick.',
	'i_thanks_title' => 'Thank You',
