	'i_wall_sub' => 'Nine frames from Bay A and Bay B',
	'i_work_lede' => 'A survey of recent commercial productions photographed on our sweeps and lifestyle sets at Wharf Yard. We work across skincare, ceramics, knitwear, beverages, and design goods.',
	'i_work_s1_h' => 'Alder & Moss: Forty-Eight Skincare Bottles on One Sweep',
	'i_work_s1_p' => 'Alder & Moss commissioned Kirinuki Studio to shoot their full skincare catalogue in Bay A. The production required uniform lighting and exact colour fidelity across 48 glass bottles in both clear and pale amber finishes. Working with lead photographer Dev Raman and digital tech Marta Okonkwo, our team established a single overhead softbox configuration on the six-metre sweep. By running tethered capture throughout the 09:00 to 17:00 shoot day, every bottle was checked for label alignment and reflection control. Deliverables included 96 catalogue views, an online gallery in 3 working days, and final files in 5 working days.',
	'i_work_s2_h' => 'Kestrel Ceramics: Tableware in Natural Daylight',
	'i_work_s2_p' => 'Kestrel Ceramics booked a lifestyle set day in Bay B to launch an artisanal tableware collection. Prop and set stylist Sofia Laine sourced washed neutral linens, stone backgrounds, and muted kitchen accessories to complement the warm ceramic glazes. Utilizing Bay B\'s generous window exposure, Lukas Brenner balanced natural morning daylight with soft reflectors to highlight surface ridges and unglazed rims. The session yielded 30 finished editorial and tabletop compositions showing the ceramics in natural use. The proofing gallery went live within 3 working days, followed by final colour-graded deliverables within 5 working days.',
	'i_work_s3_h' => 'Oriel Knit: Forty Jumpers and Six Video Loops',
	'i_work_s3_p' => 'Oriel Knit booked an apparel day in Bay A alongside our video loop add-on to photograph their winter knitwear line. Dev Raman and Marta Okonkwo captured 40 wool jumpers on our ghost mannequin, shooting front and back perspectives alongside fine weave close-ups. To give their digital storefront dynamic motion, our crew filmed six short loops of 6 seconds on the same lighting rig, capturing the natural swing and drape of the heavy knits. As with all studio commissions, the review gallery arrived in 3 working days, and final retouched files delivered in 5 working days.',
	'i_work_s4_h' => 'Recent Projects Across Our Studio Bays',
	'i_work_s4_p' => 'Beyond our featured case studies, Kirinuki Studio regularly photographs product lines for emerging and established commercial brands, including loose leaf tea packaging for Holloway Tea and utility hardware for Salt Lane Goods. Whether capturing high-volume e-commerce packshots on Bay A\'s white paper sweep or editorial table scenes in Bay B, our process remains focused on repeatability, calm communication, and tethered precision. Every client receives the same seven core day rate inclusions, fixed delivery timelines, and direct collaboration with our dedicated seven-person studio team.',
	'i_work_title' => 'Selected Commercial Work',
