	'studio_h' => 'The studio',
	'studio_lead' => 'We shoot your whole range on one sweep, in one day. You watch the first frame appear on the screen and say yes before the batch begins.',
	'studio_p1' => 'Ines Calloway opened Kirinuki Studio in 2014 with one bay and one white sweep at Wharf Yard, Harwick, after years in a catalogue house where five sets ran at once. Today there are two bays, seven people and a rule that only one thing is shot at a time.',
	'studio_p2' => 'Most of our days are packshot days: up to 60 products, two angles each, on a single sweep. The softboxes are set once, the first frame is checked against a grey card, and the rest of the range follows in the same light, so the whole catalogue matches.',
	'studio_p3' => 'Every frame is tethered to the screen on the studio floor. You can stand beside Marta, approve the first product, and ask for changes while the set is still built. The online gallery follows within three working days and final files within five.',
